{% comment %}
  Featured & Latest Articles — controlled top feed for /pages/blog

  Implements Tim's decisions of 25–26 Aug 2026.

  CONTRACT
  - Eligibility: the exact tag "featured".
  - Order: ARTICLE integer metafield custom.featured_rank, ascending.
  - Positions 1..featured_slots are rank-ordered eligible articles.
  - Remaining positions fill with the newest published non-featured articles.
  - Maximum nine cards.
  - Drafts excluded: Liquid's blog.articles exposes published articles only.
  - No duplicate articles: the ledger keys on article.id, which is globally unique.

  NO HARD-CODED ARTICLES OR BLOGS
  This file contains no article handle, ID or title, and no blog handle list.
  The candidate pool is built by iterating every blog on the store. Membership
  comes from live tag data and order comes from a live metafield. Changing the
  grid is done in Shopify, never by editing this file. The only numbers here are
  the slot counts, which are merchant settings.

  WHY `article.tags contains 'featured'` IS THE EXACT TEST
  In Liquid, `contains` applied to an ARRAY tests for an exact element match.
  article.tags is an array, so this matches only the literal tag "featured" and
  will NOT match legacy values such as "featured:top" or "featured:cardio".
  Do not pipe article.tags through a join filter before testing it. Joining
  converts the array to a string, which turns `contains` into a substring test
  and would pull in all fifteen legacy featured:* rows.

  HOLD BEHAVIOUR — REQUIRED, NOT OPTIONAL
  Per Tim's instruction, a missing, duplicate, non-integer or out-of-range rank
  is a HOLD and must NOT silently fall back to newest-first for an approved
  featured article. When any rank fails validation this section:
    1. does not pin any featured article into the grid, so no approved article
       is ever shown in an unapproved position;
    2. marks the grid data-feed-state="hold" with machine-readable reason codes;
    3. emits an HTML comment readback of every eligible article and its rank,
       so the HOLD is provable from view-source;
    4. renders a visible HOLD panel in the theme editor, or on any URL carrying
       ?feed_qa=1, so the state is visible during preview QA.
  The fallback is therefore explicit and evidenced, never silent.

  KNOWN LIMIT, documented and deliberately not worked around:
  blog.articles returns at most 50 articles per blog outside a paginate tag. The
  largest blog today is Buying Guides at 25, so there is no current exposure.
  This needs revisiting if any single blog passes 50 published articles.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'component-article-card.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'section-main-blog.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- style -%}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }

  .featured-feed-hold {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    border: 2px solid #b00020;
    background: #fff5f5;
    color: #b00020;
    padding: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .featured-feed-hold h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 15px; }
  .featured-feed-hold ul { margin: 8px 0 0 18px; }
{%- endstyle -%}

{%- liquid
  assign max_cards = section.settings.max_cards | default: 9
  assign featured_slots = section.settings.featured_slots | default: 6

  comment
    Candidate pool across every blog on the store. No handle list.
    Explicit limits: Liquid's for loop defaults to 50 iterations, which would
    silently drop articles from an 84-article pool.
  endcomment
  assign pool = '' | split: ''
  for store_blog in blogs limit: 500
    assign pool = pool | concat: store_blog.articles
  endfor

  assign pool_newest = pool | sort: 'published_at' | reverse

  comment
    Pass A — validate ranks on every eligible article.
    Ledgers are pipe-delimited so one value cannot substring-match another.
  endcomment
  assign eligible_count = 0
  assign seen_ranks = '|'
  assign hold_reasons = '|'
  assign rank_readback = ''

  for article in pool_newest limit: 500
    if article.tags contains 'featured'
      assign eligible_count = eligible_count | plus: 1
      assign rank_field = article.metafields.custom.featured_rank
      assign row_state = 'ok'

      if rank_field == blank
        assign row_state = 'missing_rank'
      else
        assign rank_raw = rank_field.value
        assign rank_num = rank_raw | plus: 0
        assign rank_int = rank_num | round

        if rank_num != rank_int
          assign row_state = 'non_integer_rank'
        elsif rank_num < 1 or rank_num > featured_slots
          assign row_state = 'out_of_range_rank'
        else
          assign rank_key = '|' | append: rank_int | append: '|'
          if seen_ranks contains rank_key
            assign row_state = 'duplicate_rank'
          else
            assign seen_ranks = seen_ranks | append: rank_int | append: '|'
          endif
        endif
      endif

      unless row_state == 'ok'
        assign reason_key = '|' | append: row_state | append: '|'
        unless hold_reasons contains reason_key
          assign hold_reasons = hold_reasons | append: row_state | append: '|'
        endunless
      endunless

      assign rank_display = rank_field.value | default: 'none'
      assign rank_readback = rank_readback | append: '    ' | append: article.handle | append: ' | rank=' | append: rank_display | append: ' | ' | append: row_state | append: '
'
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    An eligible set smaller than the configured slots is also a HOLD: an
    approved article is missing its tag, or the tag has not been applied yet.
  endcomment
  if eligible_count < featured_slots
    unless hold_reasons contains '|incomplete_eligible_set|'
      assign hold_reasons = hold_reasons | append: 'incomplete_eligible_set|'
    endunless
  endif

  assign feed_state = 'ok'
  if hold_reasons != '|'
    assign feed_state = 'hold'
  endif

  assign reason_list = hold_reasons | remove_first: '|' | split: '|'

  assign show_qa = false
  if request.design_mode
    assign show_qa = true
  endif
  if request.url contains 'feed_qa=1'
    assign show_qa = true
  endif

  assign rendered = '|'
  assign card_count = 0
-%}

{%- comment -%} View-source readback. Present on every render, so HOLD is provable. {%- endcomment -%}
<!-- FEATURED_FEED_READBACK
  state: {{ feed_state }}
  eligible (exact tag "featured"): {{ eligible_count }}
  featured slots: {{ featured_slots }} | max cards: {{ max_cards }}
  hold reasons: {% if reason_list.size > 0 %}{{ reason_list | join: ', ' }}{% else %}none{% endif %}
  eligible readback:
{% if rank_readback != blank %}{{ rank_readback }}{% else %}    (no eligible articles)
{% endif %}-->

<div class="main-blog page-width section-{{ section.id }}-padding">
  {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
    <h2 class="title--primary">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if section.settings.description != blank -%}
    <div class="main-blog-description">{{ section.settings.description }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div
    class="blog-articles blog-articles--featured-latest"
    data-feed-state="{{ feed_state }}"
    data-eligible-count="{{ eligible_count }}"
    data-featured-slots="{{ featured_slots }}"
    data-max-cards="{{ max_cards }}"
    data-hold-reasons="{% if reason_list.size > 0 %}{{ reason_list | join: ',' }}{% endif %}"
  >
    {%- if feed_state == 'hold' and show_qa -%}
      <div class="featured-feed-hold">
        <h3>Featured feed is on HOLD — rank data is not valid</h3>
        <p>
          No approved article has been pinned. Positions are filled with newest
          published articles only, so no approved article appears in an
          unapproved position. This panel is visible in the theme editor and on
          URLs carrying <code>?feed_qa=1</code>. It never renders for shoppers.
        </p>
        <ul>
          {%- for reason in reason_list -%}
            <li>{{ reason | replace: '_', ' ' }}</li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
        <p>
          Eligible articles carrying the exact tag: {{ eligible_count }} of {{ featured_slots }} expected.
          Full per-article readback is in the FEATURED_FEED_READBACK comment in page source.
        </p>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Pass 1 — rank-ordered featured articles. Only runs when every rank is
      valid. Iterating the slot numbers rather than a list of articles keeps
      the order data-driven with no hard-coded articles.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if feed_state == 'ok' -%}
      {%- for position in (1..featured_slots) -%}
        {%- if card_count >= max_cards -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- for article in pool_newest limit: 500 -%}
          {%- if article.tags contains 'featured' -%}
            {%- assign this_rank = article.metafields.custom.featured_rank.value | plus: 0 -%}
            {%- if this_rank == position -%}
              {%- assign key = '|' | append: article.id | append: '|' -%}
              {%- unless rendered contains key -%}
                {% render 'article-card',
                  article: article,
                  media_height: section.settings.image_height,
                  media_aspect_ratio: article.image.aspect_ratio,
                  show_image: section.settings.show_image,
                  show_date: section.settings.show_date,
                  show_author: section.settings.show_author,
                  show_excerpt: true
                %}
                {%- liquid
                  assign rendered = rendered | append: article.id | append: '|'
                  assign card_count = card_count | plus: 1
                -%}
              {%- endunless -%}
              {%- break -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} Pass 2 — fill remaining positions with newest non-featured articles. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- for article in pool_newest limit: 500 -%}
      {%- if card_count >= max_cards -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- unless article.tags contains 'featured' -%}
        {%- assign key = '|' | append: article.id | append: '|' -%}
        {%- unless rendered contains key -%}
          {% render 'article-card',
            article: article,
            media_height: section.settings.image_height,
            media_aspect_ratio: article.image.aspect_ratio,
            show_image: section.settings.show_image,
            show_date: section.settings.show_date,
            show_author: section.settings.show_author,
            show_excerpt: true
          %}
          {%- liquid
            assign rendered = rendered | append: article.id | append: '|'
            assign card_count = card_count | plus: 1
          -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Featured & Latest",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Featured & Latest Articles"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "description",
      "label": "Section description"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Eligibility is the exact tag 'featured'. Order is the article metafield custom.featured_rank, ascending. Legacy tags such as 'featured:top' are ignored. Remaining positions fill with the newest published articles."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "featured_slots",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 9,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "Ranked featured positions",
      "default": 6,
      "info": "Valid featured_rank values are 1 to this number. Anything outside it is a HOLD."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "max_cards",
      "min": 3,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "Maximum cards",
      "default": 9
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_image", "default": true, "label": "Show image" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_date", "default": true, "label": "Show date" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_author", "default": false, "label": "Show author" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_height",
      "options": [
        { "value": "adapt", "label": "Adapt" },
        { "value": "small", "label": "Small" },
        { "value": "medium", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "large", "label": "Large" }
      ],
      "default": "medium",
      "label": "Image height"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Top padding",
      "default": 36
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Bottom padding",
      "default": 36
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Featured & Latest" }]
}
{% endschema %}
